## What the patch is
A byte-exact FORWARD `git show 3d042c8 -- triggarr/models/config.py`. It ADDS an
already-shipped, clean config-validation feature: a new `shutdown_drain_timeout`
field on GeneralConfig declared `Field(default=60.0, ge=1.0, allow_inf_nan=False)`
— ge=1.0 rejects zero/negative (a typo cannot disable the drain), and
allow_inf_nan=False rejects inf/nan (ge=1.0 alone accepts +inf in pydantic v2).
This is defect-free feature code — reviewing it should produce NO critical/warning
finding. Safe ON the input-validation axis: the field is bounds-guarded tighter
than the surrounding existing fields; it introduces no leak, no injection, no
resource issue. (The deliberate absence of a model-level upper bound is documented
in the commit body — the form clamp is the UI ceiling and the env override is a
shutdown-time escape hatch.)

